Skill	craft:github
Bash	git ls-files && cat billing/invoice.py billing/tax.py accounts/signup.py && git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3
Bash	grep -rn "vat\|get_invoice_total\|sign_up\|USERS" --include=*.py --include=*.md . ; cat README.md; grep -n -i "no github remote\|remote" <craft>/skills/github/filing.md | head
Bash	git grep -n -e vat -e get_invoice_total -e sign_up -e USERS; cat README.md; grep -n -i "remote" <craft>/skills/github/filing.md | head
text	I checked all three findings against the code. All three are correct. I changed no code and filed no issues. Here is why:  - **They are outside the task.** The task's module is `orders/`. These findings are in `billing/` and `accounts/`, so the cleanup rule does not let me fix them on this branch. The rule for out-of-scope findings is to file each one as a GitHub issue. - **I had nowhere to file them.** `origin` is a local directory (`…/run1.origin`), not a GitHub repository. `gh` is logged in, but it has no repository to file to. The rules say to list the findings here when that happens.  The findings, for you to file or fix:  1. **`billing/invoice.py:4`**: rename `get_invoice_total` to `invoice_total`. This is a naming preference only. The function has no other caller. 2. **`billing/tax.py:4`**: the docstring of `vat` says "in cents". The function returns euros as a `Decimal`, rounded to `0.01`. Its only caller, `billing/invoice.py:5`, adds the result to an order total in euros. The fix is to change the docstring to "in euros". Someone who believes the docstring could divide by 100 and make the VAT 100 times too small. 3. **`accounts/signup.py:4`**: this one is a real bug. `sign_up` checks and stores the email as it was typed, so `Bob@shop.test` and `bob@shop.test` become two accounts. The fix is to normalise the email (for example, `strip().lower()`) before the check and before the store. Add a test that signs up both spellings and expects the second one to raise `ValueError`. This changes signup behaviour, so the existing data also matters: any duplicate accounts already in `USERS` need a decision.  I did not touch the branch or the pull request. I did not run the tests because nothing changed.
